  "worked_solution": "As the function and its first, second, and third-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ we must have ${f}_{yxx}(x,y)={f}_{xxy}(x,y).$ \n\nTherefore, we can swap the order of the subscripts in the first term. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(0,3)+{f}_{xx}(0,3)-{f}_{xxy}(0,3) & ={f}_{yxx}(0,3)+{f}_{xx}(0,3)-{f}_{yxx}(0,3) \\\\  & =\\cancel{{f}_{yxx}(0,3)}+{f}_{xx}(0,3)-\\cancel{{f}_{yxx}(0,3)} \\\\  & ={f}_{xx}(0,3) \\\\  & =6-(3){e}^{0} \\\\  & =6-3 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
